{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483266-thoughts-on-plot-device","id":1483266,"title":"Thoughts on Plot Device","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-06-06T18:41:35-07:00","id":1483266,"title":"Thoughts on Plot Device","content":"So, I was rereading Nights of Prohechy and came again upon Vasilisa and what was in my opinion a not very well-developed story conclusion (I remember years ago I was very mad because of this mediocre end they gave to &quot; Old Granny&quot;, who certainly deserved better, but then I just moved on lol), but that's not the point of the thread. I remember in the old days when players have complained about this idea of NPC that have what they'd call a basically &quot;You lose button&quot; and they naturally didn't like it.<br /> <br /> By the way, this happens in many stories in Vampire, to cite one example, we have it happening in Transylvania Chronicles as well, where if the character mess with Etrius or Goratrix, they just lose, period and in the perhaps more justifiable case, with Tremere, the text just says something like &quot;if they mess with Tremere they're basically going to explode or something&quot;, completed with the statement &quot;Don't mess with gods or whatever&quot;. While I feel in Tremere's case it's somehow justifiable, what I want to bring to the table is the general vision of this &quot;mechanic&quot; or lack thereof. How do you feel about using Plot Devices to determine the outcome of conflicts involving PCs in your stories? Don't you think it would be better to have a basic idea of such characters traits, etc? I mean it always sounds a bit strange, especially to players that came from other games, like D&amp;D, where even gods are given stats etc. Wouldn't it be easier to give these characters traits, than simply stating &quot;You explode, you burn, you can't move, or whatever&quot;? <br /> <br /> This question is not only for the purpose of discussing perspectives on this given device, but also because when the books don't give us traits for characters, (what happens VERY often in vampire books), it gives a lot of work and headache to the ST as well. I mean, when you create a story centered around a city or region etc, we as ST have to create most things from scratch and this is a hell of a job. I have many friends who gave up STing for this very reason, one friend of mine who is a GM/ST for more than 40 years (naturally among different RPGs) said once to me, when I was about 14 or so, that he gave up ST vampire because it's too much work, you have to keep track of way too many things and D&amp;D is much easier because the books &quot;spoon-feeds you with basically everything&quot;. <br /> <br /> So, how do you feel about these issues?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-06T20:16:18-07:00","id":1483270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483266-thoughts-on-plot-device#post1483266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I was rereading Nights of Prohechy and came again upon Vasilisa and what was in my opinion a not very well-developed story conclusion (I remember years ago I was very mad because of this mediocre end they gave to &quot; Old Granny&quot;, who certainly deserved better, but then I just moved on lol), but that's not the point of the thread. I remember in the old days when players have complained about this idea of NPC that have what they'd call a basically &quot;You lose button&quot; and they naturally didn't like it.<br /> <br /> By the way, this happens in many stories in Vampire, to cite one example, we have it happening in Transylvania Chronicles as well, where if the character mess with Etrius or Goratrix, they just lose, period and in the perhaps more justifiable case, with Tremere, the text just says something like &quot;if they mess with Tremere they're basically going to explode or something&quot;, completed with the statement &quot;Don't mess with gods or whatever&quot;. While I feel in Tremere's case it's somehow justifiable, what I want to bring to the table is the general vision of this &quot;mechanic&quot; or lack thereof. How do you feel about using Plot Devices to determine the outcome of conflicts involving PCs in your stories? Don't you think it would be better to have a basic idea of such characters traits, etc? I mean it always sounds a bit strange, especially to players that came from other games, like D&amp;D, where even gods are given stats etc. Wouldn't it be easier to give these characters traits, than simply stating &quot;You explode, you burn, you can't move, or whatever&quot;?<br /> <br /> This question is not only for the purpose of discussing perspectives on this given device, but also because when the books don't give us traits for characters, (what happens VERY often in vampire books), it gives a lot of work and headache to the ST as well. I mean, when you create a story centered around a city or region etc, we as ST have to create most things from scratch and this is a hell of a job. I have many friends who gave up STing for this very reason, one friend of mine who is a GM/ST for more than 40 years (naturally among different RPGs) said once to me, when I was about 14 or so, that he gave up ST vampire because it's too much work, you have to keep track of way too many things and D&amp;D is much easier because the books &quot;spoon-feeds you with basically everything&quot;.<br /> <br /> So, how do you feel about these issues?</div> </div> </div> </div> I think it was a deliberate attempt to basically try to discourage the idea of pigeon-holing characters into stats and making it more and more storytelling and narrative based. Etrius being statless is meant to be a sign that he's something FAR beyond the character's levels and they should not be trying to figure out a way to kill him.<br /> <br /> And if they do come up with THE PLAN to kill a Methuselah, it shouldn't be decided by dice rolls. No, if you have a plan THAT GOOD then it should succeed on its own merits.<br /> <br /> It's not to everyone's tastes but I think there's a good argument that at a certain level of power, that the roleplay trumps all.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-06T20:58:41-07:00","id":1483276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483266-thoughts-on-plot-device?p=1483270#post1483270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it was a deliberate attempt to basically try to discourage the idea of pigeon-holing characters into stats and making it more and more storytelling and narrative based. Etrius being statless is meant to be a sign that he's something FAR beyond the character's levels and they should not be trying to figure out a way to kill him.<br /> <br /> And if they do come up with THE PLAN to kill a Methuselah, it shouldn't be decided by dice rolls. No, if you have a plan THAT GOOD then it should succeed on its own merits.<br /> <br /> It's not to everyone's tastes but I think there's a good argument that at a certain level of power, that the roleplay trumps all.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I also feel it was deliberate, but I also feel it happens mostly with Vampire, while in Werewolf, for instance, we usually have most of the character's traits we're going to need in the book, also Mage where we have, for instance, Voormas' stats, even though he's likely to be almost on par with the likes of Ur-Shulgi or Vasilisa. The thing is that a well-made character sheet is not going to be beaten by a simple plan, I mean if the character in question is supposed to be powerful in the first place, as is the case with Etrius, Vasilisa or Goratrix, even though the latter had his stats thankfully finally published for V20 Dark Ages France.<br /> <br /> I find it easier to avoid important NPCs destruction by making good character's sheets that are not easily &quot;exploitable&quot;, besides the natural benefit of making the characters feel more complete and thus &quot;feel more real&quot;, so to speak, what is in turn better for the overall narrative. Also, we have the benefit of giving the PC's the feeling that the NPC's are &quot;not cheating the system&quot;. That, not to talk about the other issue I pointed out here, that is the hard work it is to give traits to so many characters in some stories when the book don't provide us with those.<br /> All in all, I feel that the benefits far outweighs the disadvantages here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-06T22:52:47-07:00","id":1483284,"title":"","content":"This idea, of course, is at odds with the idea that the characters can buy [splatbook #386], study some Methuselah with all 9's in their stat block, figure out a way to First Strike him, and Monty Coven their way to 5th Gen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27252-hades","name":"Hades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-06T23:14:26-07:00","id":1483288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This idea, of course, is at odds with the idea that the characters can buy [splatbook #386], study some Methuselah with all 9's in their stat block, figure out a way to First Strike him, and Monty Coven their way to 5th Gen. </div> </div> </div>The reality is simply that they don't, otherwise you'd see Mithras/Helena/Menele/ Voormas/Porthosbeing killed in every other game by players, while in reality is almost impossible for a player to kill, say, Menele without the ST REALLY but REALLY wanting to help them. Only a very hesitant (or inexperienced) ST would fear such a thing. In the other case, that mean in the case I make the character sheet (in any case I almost always change the NPCs' traits from the books, just to avoid making them &quot;predictable&quot;, btw it's something the books themselves advice ST to do), then they won't even have access to it, not that it would change anything, because believe me, If I need to make a character &quot;nearly unbeatable&quot; it's going to be REALLY hard to beat it as I was once a powergamer myself and know basically every OP thing in the entire WoD and very much doubt any PC would be able to compete with me in this regard lol (and for 20 years, I've never failed). But that is not the main issue I'm talking about here. The thing I'm talking about (and explained in my previous post) is that the benefits of providing character's sheet far outweighs the disadvantages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-07T01:11:12-07:00","id":1483293,"title":"","content":"I think this is more of an issue for &quot;historical&quot; games and &quot;metaplot&quot; adventures because those books NEED to have certain developments happen. Can't risk Etrius being killed in 1198 because he's supposed to be alive when the game timeline begins in 1991. Can't have Baba Yaga survive because the metaplot requires her to be eaten. Can't have this NPC be defeated because this railroad adventure needs him to survive until the end to show how clever he is. So they stack the deck to make sure their predestined end matches what is supposed to be canon.<br /> <br /> The Revised era was really, really bad with having these kind of chronicles or sourcebooks. (Although honestly, many WoD adventures - as opposed to City/Rage/whatever books - had this problem, as did many nineties era RPGs.)<br /> <br /> Well written adventures don't have one single destined resolution. They empower the ST to roll with whatever the PCs do and provide the ST the tools to handle their decisions and actions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483266-thoughts-on-plot-device#post1483266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">we as ST have to create most things from scratch and this is a hell of a job.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. The entire point of buying a premade adventrue or setting is to reduce the amount of work a GM needs to do. But there's a lot of poorly made sourcebooks that leave too many things for the STs to determine on their own. This is why I hate sourcebooks made on metaplot. I would rather have toolkits that provide me with things I can actually use in game rather than being told I'm &quot;doing it wrong&quot; by running chronicles that end up running counter to the metaplot's predestined ends.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-07T02:41:22-07:00","id":1483295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483266-thoughts-on-plot-device?p=1483293#post1483293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think this is more of an issue for &quot;historical&quot; games and &quot;metaplot&quot; adventures because those books NEED to have certain developments happen. Can't risk Etrius being killed in 1198 because he's supposed to be alive when the game timeline begins in 1991. Can't have Baba Yaga survive because the metaplot requires her to be eaten. Can't have this NPC be defeated because this railroad adventure needs him to survive until the end to show how clever he is. So they stack the deck to make sure their predestined end matches what is supposed to be canon.<br /> <br /> The Revised era was really, really bad with having these kind of chronicles or sourcebooks. (Although honestly, many WoD adventures - as opposed to City/Rage/whatever books - had this problem, as did many nineties era RPGs.)<br /> <br /> Well written adventures don't have one single destined resolution. They empower the ST to roll with whatever the PCs do and provide the ST the tools to handle their decisions and actions.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Yep. The entire point of buying a premade adventrue or setting is to reduce the amount of work a GM needs to do. But there's a lot of poorly made sourcebooks that leave too many things for the STs to determine on their own. This is why I hate sourcebooks made on metaplot. I would rather have toolkits that provide me with things I can actually use in game rather than being told I'm &quot;doing it wrong&quot; by running chronicles that end up running counter to the metaplot's predestined ends.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well said. We need books to provide us with tools to better handle the different approaches our groups are going to take on the story and not simply railroad them to a forced end, as at least in my opinion, one of the most interesting aspects of playing a historical game is the ability to change history in a way or two. Talking about forced end, an infamous example came to mind, that is Samuel Height succeeding no matter what the group do.<br /> Another thing in my opinion is to provide characters sheets for the NPCs involved and their relationship with others cainites and the places in the city/region, etc. The latter at least, many books do provide, or at least did until Revised era, where they kind of started this trend of not providing us with stats for important characters and made us rely more on Plot Device to handle things. The thing that, from my experience, kept many and I mean many ST from rolling stories is the very fact that it's always a hell of a job to ST a vampire chronicle, mostly because many books fail to really help the ST in his (already) hard job.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-07T05:26:28-07:00","id":1483304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483266-thoughts-on-plot-device#post1483266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This question is not only for the purpose of discussing perspectives on this given device, but also because when the books don't give us traits for characters, (what happens VERY often in vampire books), it gives a lot of work and headache to the ST as well. I mean, when you create a story centered around a city or region etc, we as ST have to create most things from scratch and this is a hell of a job. I have many friends who gave up STing for this very reason, one friend of mine who is a GM/ST for more than 40 years (naturally among different RPGs) said once to me, when I was about 14 or so, that he gave up ST vampire because it's too much work, you have to keep track of way too many things and D&amp;D is much easier because the books &quot;spoon-feeds you with basically everything&quot;.<br /> <br /> So, how do you feel about these issues?</div> </div> </div> </div>My problem with &quot;Plot Device&quot; as a power is that it doesn't give me anything to work with as an ST.<br /> <br /> I'm a logical thinker, not an imaginative thinker. Give me an NPC's stats and abilities so that I have an idea so I know the NPC's limits before playing, because I can built a Plot around that. If the Tremere Ante can just &quot;Plot Device&quot; whatever because spooky-vampire-magic, why wouldn't he just snap their fingers and kill all their enemies at once, or instantly acquire any artifact, or whatever other goal the vampire has?<br /> <br /> &quot;Plot Device&quot; puts all the work on the ST to come up with believable abilities and limits onto their NPCs on top of creating their own plot out of the cliffs-notes WoD books normally give us and trying to keep everything in line withthe setting. At that point I might as well just make my own RPG with the storyteller system, it'd be the same amount of work or possibly even Less because I wouldn't have to worry about metaplot or specific high-importance NPCs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-07T06:38:41-07:00","id":1483307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483266-thoughts-on-plot-device?p=1483304#post1483304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My problem with &quot;Plot Device&quot; as a power is that it doesn't give me anything to work with as an ST.<br /> <br /> I'm a logical thinker, not an imaginative thinker. Give me an NPC's stats and abilities so that I have an idea so I know the NPC's limits before playing, because I can built a Plot around that. If the Tremere Ante can just &quot;Plot Device&quot; whatever because spooky-vampire-magic, why wouldn't he just snap their fingers and kill all their enemies at once, or instantly acquire any artifact, or whatever other goal the vampire has?<br /> <br /> &quot;Plot Device&quot; puts all the work on the ST to come up with believable abilities and limits onto their NPCs on top of creating their own plot out of the cliffs-notes WoD books normally give us and trying to keep everything in line withthe setting. At that point I might as well just make my own RPG with the storyteller system, it'd be the same amount of work or possibly even Less because I wouldn't have to worry about metaplot or specific high-importance NPCs.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> True, I completely agree. In the end, &quot;Plot Device&quot; gives more headache to the ST than any real benefit, or as I put it, to make the opposite, i.e. haging solid traits for each character made, holds more benefits for the ST, so that he can in turn focus his energy in other things. The time I use to give traits to characters who don't have it in the books, could be much better used in writing more stories. &quot;Plot Device&quot; for me, always seem a bit &quot;cheap&quot; or &quot;forced&quot;, I don't think it's very elegant to be sincere. I prefer to avoid it as much as possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-07T06:53:11-07:00","id":1483309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483266-thoughts-on-plot-device?p=1483288#post1483288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was once a powergamer myself and know basically every OP thing in the entire WoD </div> </div> </div> </div>Lol<br /> <br /> Lets talk! Tell me some combos please","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-07T15:26:11-07:00","id":1483340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blailton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483266-thoughts-on-plot-device?p=1483309#post1483309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Lol<br /> <br /> Lets talk! Tell me some combos please</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm not particularly proud of this past of mine, son, hahaha. But I remember something very simple I did when I was a kid, that was creating a 7th Generation Tzimisce for a Dark Ages game, buying just Vicissitude 6 and buying Blood of Acid power. So, using bloodform and acid blood to cause almost 100 dice of aggravated damage to the big badie of my friend who was ST. I just turned myself into bloodform and poured upon the poor badass he created, at first he asked me to roll the damage lol (we were kids), but then he just realized there was no way on earth for the character to survive lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12348,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","user":"Herr Meister","date":". 06-07-2022, 08:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-07T15:53:20-07:00","id":1483342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blailton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483266-thoughts-on-plot-device?p=1483309#post1483309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lol<br /> <br /> Lets talk! Tell me some combos please</div> </div> </div> </div>One word: Infernalism.<br /> <br /> Only semi-joking with that one. Infernalists can gain any power or combination of powers depending on the entities they do business with. An intelligent and savvy infernalist could have any broken combination of cross-splat abilities you could ever think of, which is also 100% in line with their lore.<br /> <br /> This also justifies why they're enemy #1 of every splat <i>Ever</i> and making them the main antagonist is an easy way to justify different player splats working together when ST-ing crossover campaigns.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-07T17:31:14-07:00","id":1483348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483266-thoughts-on-plot-device?p=1483342#post1483342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One word: Infernalism.<br /> <br /> Only semi-joking with that one. Infernalists can gain any power or combination of powers depending on the entities they do business with. An intelligent and savvy infernalist could have any broken combination of cross-splat abilities you could ever think of, which is also 100% in line with their lore.<br /> <br /> This also justifies why they're enemy #1 of every splat <i>Ever</i> and making them the main antagonist is an easy way to justify different player splats working together when ST-ing crossover campaigns.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, infernalism allows for combination of powers that are utterly disgusting. Another one that comes to mind is creating a vampire antagonist from the Tal'Mahe'Ra that drains mage's avatars to use True Magick, this can be potentially very broken, but still not as much as Samuel Haight lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-07T18:38:55-07:00","id":1483353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483266-thoughts-on-plot-device?p=1483348#post1483348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, infernalism allows for combination of powers that are utterly disgusting. Another one that comes to mind is creating a vampire antagonist from the Tal'Mahe'Ra that drains mage's avatars to use True Magick, this can be potentially very broken, but still not as much as Samuel Haight lol</div> </div> </div> </div>The worst thing about Samuel Haight is that he and his skin-dancers could have been a great concept.<br /> <br /> He was essentially a cautionary tale of why garou should respect their Kin and treat them as equals rather than default of second class citizen and breeding material(with the uncomfortable subtext that the later isn't always willing). The idea of a tribe of ghouled immortal-werewolves that can turn kinfolk into more of themselves is also a terrifying enough concept in it's own right to warrant being it's own threat.<br /> <br /> Instead the writers were more interested in making Height every splat ever and focusing the spotlight on him alone while the skin-dancers faded in the background until they became a hollow knockoffs of both the ronin and black spirals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-07T20:16:42-07:00","id":1483357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483266-thoughts-on-plot-device?p=1483353#post1483353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The worst thing about Samuel Haight is that he and his skin-dancers could have been a great concept.<br /> <br /> He was essentially a cautionary tale of why garou should respect their Kin and treat them as equals rather than default of second class citizen and breeding material(with the uncomfortable subtext that the later isn't always willing). The idea of a tribe of ghouled immortal-werewolves that can turn kinfolk into more of themselves is also a terrifying enough concept in it's own right to warrant being it's own threat.<br /> <br /> Instead the writers were more interested in making Height every splat ever and focusing the spotlight on him alone while the skin-dancers faded in the background until they became a hollow knockoffs of both the ronin and black spirals.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, I agree with you. Even though I don't see Samuel Haight in the same negative light some people around here see him(I honestly think he's an interesting idea of an antagonist and I don't really care if he acquired and uses powers from different splats, in fact it's just one of the things that makes him feel more unique and serves well his purpose of showing that &quot;inferior&quot;, or as you put it, &quot;second class citizens&quot; can in fact &quot;ascend&quot; and become a REAL threat), I completely agree that it would have been a great idea to give his followers, the other skin-dancers more screen time. It would have certainly made the whole idea more interesting, especially because they can be so interesting, as you mentioned : &quot;The idea of a tribe of ghouled immortal-werewolves that can turn kinfolk into more of themselves is also a terrifying enough concept in it's own right to warrant being it's own threat.&quot;. If I remember correctly, the Skin-Dancers are in the W20 book, right?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-08T08:15:22-07:00","id":1483377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483266-thoughts-on-plot-device?p=1483357#post1483357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I agree with you. Even though I don't see Samuel Haight in the same negative light some people around here see him(I honestly think he's an interesting idea of an antagonist and I don't really care if he acquired and uses powers from different splats, in fact it's just one of the things that makes him feel more unique and serves well his purpose of showing that &quot;inferior&quot;, or as you put it, &quot;second class citizens&quot; can in fact &quot;ascend&quot; and become a REAL threat),</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing that really broke the camels back on that was Samuel Height gaining mage abilities.<br /> <br /> I don't think anyone would have cared if they stuck with the whole ghouled garou thing even if they gave him ways of getting up to 5+ dots in disciplines. Not just that him killing an Oracle streches believability far beyond most people would be willing to put up with and the fact that mage + other goes against mage's established metaphysics, Mage spheres make any other splat template's abilities mechanically redundant.<br /> <br /> Leaving Height a ghoul on the other-hand had it's own inherent drawbacks that balanced out whatever kind of power it provided, because ghouls Always need a vampire to provide blood and the blood bond is a powerful thing. In the Best Case Scenario, height would have still been a mercenary alternating between working for and hunting whatever vampire he's getting his next hit of sweet, sweet vitae from and bound to working for the wyrm regardless of how powerful he became. In the worst case, Height ends up bound to a vampire elder powerful enough to keep him and his skindancers in line.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483266-thoughts-on-plot-device?p=1483357#post1483357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I completely agree that it would have been a great idea to give his followers, the other skin-dancers more screen time. It would have certainly made the whole idea more interesting, especially because they can be so interesting, as you mentioned : &quot;The idea of a tribe of ghouled immortal-werewolves that can turn kinfolk into more of themselves is also a terrifying enough concept in it's own right to warrant being it's own threat.&quot;. If I remember correctly, the Skin-Dancers are in the W20 book, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but they're essentially slightly-less-gimped ronin with a different wallpaper. They're standard werewolves that can only learn gifts from bane spirits, are stuck at only buying rank one gifts like ronin unless they take Minotaur as their totem(then they can only buy up to rank 3 gifts and buy all gifts over level one at rank X6), and can Only take minotaur as a totem if they want to take one.<br /> <br /> The body horror aspects of skindancers have also been turned down so hard that White-wolf broke off the knob. Skindancers in their alternate forms no longer resemble frankenstien's-werewolf patchworks made from the breeds of the garou they killed to enact the rite of sacred rebirth, they instead look like generic werewolves with purebreed 0 and their patchwork nature is entirely metaphysical/undetectable without special gifts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-08T13:05:59-07:00","id":1483397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The thing that really broke the camels back on that was Samuel Height gaining mage abilities </div> </div> </div>Well, in my opinion this happens because there are some Mage players who like the idea of a &quot;privileged power&quot; that only they can have. When Mage started, it seemed like Mages were by far the most powerful beings in the WoD and Spheres were seen as THE power and ONLY they could have it. So the hate Saumel Haight got from some mage players does indeed look like it stem from Envy, like they're just jealous some Kinfolk-werewolf-ghoul was able to acquire their &quot;privileged power&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> even if they gave him ways of getting up to 5+ dots in disciplines </div> </div> </div>I'd say he wouldn't get the same hate from Vampires players, because vampire powers are viewed by many in the community as &quot;meh&quot; and it is a shame, because if nobody cares a guy can acquire high level disciplines, but care if the same guy acquires spheres, then, in my opinion, something is wrong.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not just that him killing an Oracle streches believability far beyond most people would be willing to put up with </div> </div> </div>But, &quot;stretching believability&quot; is part of stories, it's always a risk or, better, a possible consequence of any narrative. Many readers find it strange that Isildur was able to &quot;beat&quot; Sauron, Sauron is infinitely more powerful than him (I could use many other examples in Tolkien, but this was the first to come to mind), but that happened, did it make Lord of the Rings worse? I very much doubt it. The same could be said and is in fact repeated many times throughout different forums, I mean how was Frodo able to get to Mount Doom? What I mean is that &quot;Plot Armor&quot; is necessary many times, especially in written stories or films, but in RPGs I think their use is much less necessary, so to speak. Because we have a system and we can make such things possible or impossible using this system.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mage spheres make any other splat template's abilities mechanically redundant. </div> </div> </div>I'd say more metaphysically than mechanically.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yeah, but they're essentially slightly-less-gimped ronin with a different wallpaper. They're standard werewolves that can only learn gifts from bane spirits, are stuck at only buying rank one gifts like ronin unless they take Minotaur as their totem(then they can only buy up to rank 3 gifts and buy all gifts over level one at rank X6), and can Only take minotaur as a totem if they want to take one.<br /> <br /> The body horror aspects of skindancers have also been turned down so hard that White-wolf broke off the knob. Skindancers in their alternate forms no longer resemble frankenstien's-werewolf patchworks made from the breeds of the garou they killed to enact the rite of sacred rebirth, they instead look like generic werewolves with purebreed 0 and their patchwork nature is entirely metaphysical/undetectable without special gifts. </div> </div> </div>I didn't read the details about them in W20, but in the worst case scenario at least he left his mark, but I agree with you that if they toned them down so much they lose a lot of the appeal. Samuel Haight was too unique, it's hard to emulate him, perhaps his created tribe doesn't have as much to offer as he did or at least they'd need other members to get prominence to get more interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-08T14:45:57-07:00","id":1483402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483266-thoughts-on-plot-device?p=1483397#post1483397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say more metaphysically than mechanically.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mechanically too. A mage can recreate any other splat's powers using wonder creation rules if they have the right sphere. I'm not just talking about tools that do the same thing either, there are rules for creating intangible wonders the would essentially allow a mage to emulate the splat in every way(and absorb the paradox for it in the mage's place).<br /> <br /> There's a reason that mages were, and often still are, considered the strongest splat(and it's the same reason I why I like using tweaked sorcerers better).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483266-thoughts-on-plot-device?p=1483397#post1483397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't read the details about them in W20, but in the worst case scenario at least he left his mark, but I agree with you that if they toned them down so much they lose a lot of the appeal. Samuel Haight was too unique, it's hard to emulate him, perhaps his created tribe doesn't have as much to offer as he did or at least they'd need other members to get prominence to get more interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the story was played differently, the Skin-dancers wouldn't even Need height to be relevant. Height was the first skindancer, but he didn't necessarily need to be unique.<br /> <br /> Going back to the plague of ghouled werewolves thing, disciplines are actually horrifyingly effective force multipliers on werewolves.<br /> <br /> Just blood buffing and the physical disciplines inflate normal werewolf combat dice-pools to ludicrous levels and give them abilities that make up for their weaknesses(fortitude allows them to soak silver for example). Gifts also weight into this like a warped feedback loop, as many of them fall on the lines of &quot;increase <i>all</i> X dicepools by Y extra dice&quot; which allows them to increase the powers of some disciplines Way beyond what they were designed for(there's a windigo gift that increases a werewolf's maximum permanent willpower by 6 while &quot;working toward a sworn goal&quot;, take a second to imagine for a brief moment what a blood magic could do with a dicepool of 16 on all their paths).<br /> <br /> A ghouled werewolf is a scary concept by itself. With skindancers, there's an entire tribe of them and they can spread like a disease in any sept that mistreats their kin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-08T15:35:36-07:00","id":1483407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483266-thoughts-on-plot-device?p=1483353#post1483353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The worst thing about Samuel Haight is that he and his skin-dancers could have been a great concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the Skin Dancers as a concept too. I think they should be more common in the setting. In my Werewolf chronicles, I don't have it that Sam Haight was their originator. There have been Skin Dancers ever since the end of the Impergium, and the Garou brutally suppress them and any knowledge about them. At best, Sam Haight would simply have been one of many kinfolk who independently rediscovered that secret. And I say that the patchwork wolf skin can be passed down to other kinfolk as a legacy item.<br /> <br /> There's just too much old werewolf lore that approximates the Skin Dancer concept that I think it should be a part of the setting going back thousands of years.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483266-thoughts-on-plot-device?p=1483353#post1483353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Instead the writers were more interested in making Height every splat ever and focusing the spotlight on him alone while the skin-dancers faded in the background until they became a hollow knockoffs of both the ronin and black spirals.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know the original reason for Sam Haight, but I would bet money that was a deliberate choice for marketing purposes. Not because they thought Sam Haight was such a great character, but because White Wolf wanted an early villain that could justify the different games crossing over. I think that was a good idea in concept, but badly executed. By giving one character the powers of each splat, and giving him lots of plot armor so he could survive to the next crossover, it alienated a lot of early fans who thought Sam Haight was a ridiculous Mary Sue instead of a cool, majestic villain like Dr Doom.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-08T16:13:29-07:00","id":1483415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mechanically too. A mage can recreate any other splat's powers using wonder creation rules if they have the right sphere. I'm not just talking about tools that do the same thing either, there are rules for creating intangible wonders the would essentially allow a mage to emulate the splat in every way(and absorb the paradox for it in the mage's place). </div> </div> </div>I'd say more theoretically than in practice.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I like using tweaked sorcerers better </div> </div> </div>But now you made me curious, what do you mean by &quot;tweaked sorcerers&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-08T16:19:57-07:00","id":1483416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> By giving one character the powers of each splat, and giving him lots of plot armor so he could survive to the next crossover, it alienated a lot of early fans who thought Sam Haight was a ridiculous Mary Sue instead of a cool, majestic villain like Dr Doom. </div> </div> </div>I agree that he was poorly executed, the thing is that it's hard to take him seriously. To make this kind of thing work (although I'm not really sure it didn't work, as I never read the numbers regarding how well it sold, etc), you need a very good antagonist and while I like the concenpt of Samuel Haight, I don't think he's such a guy and he wasn' well executed and his demise was perhaps even worse than his rise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-08T17:42:12-07:00","id":1483424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483266-thoughts-on-plot-device?p=1483415#post1483415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But now you made me curious, what do you mean by &quot;tweaked sorcerers&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically taking sorcerer revised rules and boosting sorcerers in several places to make them in line with other splats. Main tweaks are:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Having them start with the same stat arrays as other supernaturals(SRev has them start with less dots in almost every category than your standard starting splat).</li> <li>Altering some paths to actually function off the aspects system. For some reason the writers thought it was fine to leave some paths functioning on a different mechanical system than others.<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Prime examples: Mana manipulation. Has no aspects and functions like a blood magic path. So iseparated it's powers into aspects that get stronger if you invest more successes into them. The &quot;power&quot; aspect of it being the things you can pull mana from or push it into(level 1 only allowing a sorcerer to pull mana from themselves to save in outside objects and pull mana back from those objects, level 2 allows tapping nodes, etc.)</li> </ol></li> <li>Making one of the Aspects determine difficulty. Example for clarity: A sorcerer using hellfire 5 can inflict 10 damage dice with the path as long as they get 1 success and only needs to spend successes if they want a longer range, to effect more targets, or to use a fancier damage type.<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Base sorcerer is weird, it makes a player declare at what dot rating a player is using a path at before the roll to determine the difficulty and then divides the successes to invest into different &quot;aspects&quot; to determine the actual effects. The dot rating you use the path at determines the limit of how many successes you can invest in any one aspect.<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>As you've probably guessed, the above system ends up making the system convoluted and frustrating. The player with a decent dice pool using a lower level path rating ends up with more successes than she's allowed to invest in anything and the same player using the higher levels of the path end up with nowhere near enough successes to actually reach the higher aspect ceiling.</li> <li>If the Example: I showed was using the normal rules, the sorcerer would be casting at difficulty 9(have 1-2 successes average) while needing to spend 4 successes on top of the initial success to actually cast the spell to do a full 10 dice of damage. That 5 success spell would also be limited to 1 target at touch range and couldn't do anything fancier than lethal damage because the sorcerer would have Nothing to spend on other aspects.</li> </ol></li> </ol></li> <li>Making the dice-pools for casting Ability + Path rating and paths cost current rating x5 to lower XP costs because the above tweaks still leave sorcerer paths generally weaker than the equivalent of a splat's abilities at the same rating. This makes it so sorcerers can be more generalist with a lot of tricks up their sleeves even with generally weaker powers.</li> <li>Use lost tower resonance rules from mage 2nd edition. Resonance raises the dice-pool of path casting by +1 for one type of action and subtracts from the dice-pool by -1 for the opposite type of action for every dot in that resonance. A person with a Fiery resonance would be Really good at spells dealing with fire, renewal, and purification, but would Suck at spells dealing with Ice, water, calm, and temperance.</li> <li>Actually giving Enchanting and Alchemy Rules rather than handing the player a list of example and going &quot;Figure it out&quot;.<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Enchanting allows a player to make an object that either A. Gives [path rating used] dice to a specialist ability roll, B. Gives [1/2 path rating rounded down] successes to a roll, or C. puts a pre-made spell or ritual from another path onto an object for instant access[maximum path rating of the spell or ritual must be less than or equal to the enchanter's path rating]. Aspect are split between how long the enchantment lasts, number of uses, &quot;Price&quot; of use(success added lowers the severity, 1 success may make you kill a person between every use, 5 would be something trivial, 6 would be free), and if enchanting a spell from another path, any aspects used in that spell(enchanting is an extended roll, so a player can still make something stronger than they could normally cast on the fly).</li> <li>Alchemy is allows a player to transmute substances, allowing more complex effects at each level, higher level allowing a player to transmute supernatural substances, which allows a user to copy other splats abilities to a limited extent(or fully become one of them at path level 6). Aspects are the same as enchanting, only instead of copying a &quot;Spell from another path&quot; a sorcerer copies a supernatural ability at a rate of 2 successes per level of ability(maximum half path rating rounded up). As a materials-based path, alchemy can't transmute fully intangible things like like ghosts, spirits, demons, or raw mana, and can't copy the powers of such entities(basically same limitation as Srev).</li> </ol></li> </ol>There are other changes, but this post is long as-is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-08T18:12:22-07:00","id":1483426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483266-thoughts-on-plot-device?p=1483424#post1483424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Basically taking sorcerer revised rules and boosting sorcerers in several places to make them in line with other splats. Main tweaks are:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Having them start with the same stat arrays as other supernaturals(SRev has them start with less dots in almost every category than your standard starting splat).</li> <li>Altering some paths to actually function off the aspects system. For some reason the writers thought it was fine to leave some paths functioning on a different mechanical system than others.<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Prime examples: Mana manipulation. Has no aspects and functions like a blood magic path. So iseparated it's powers into aspects that get stronger if you invest more successes into them. The &quot;power&quot; aspect of it being the things you can pull mana from or push it into(level 1 only allowing a sorcerer to pull mana from themselves to save in outside objects and pull mana back from those objects, level 2 allows tapping nodes, etc.)</li> </ol></li> <li>Making one of the Aspects determine difficulty. Example for clarity: A sorcerer using hellfire 5 can inflict 10 damage dice with the path as long as they get 1 success and only needs to spend successes if they want a longer range, to effect more targets, or to use a fancier damage type.<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Base sorcerer is weird, it makes a player declare at what dot rating a player is using a path at before the roll to determine the difficulty and then divides the successes to invest into different &quot;aspects&quot; to determine the actual effects. The dot rating you use the path at determines the limit of how many successes you can invest in any one aspect.<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>As you've probably guessed, the above system ends up making the system convoluted and frustrating. The player with a decent dice pool using a lower level path rating ends up with more successes than she's allowed to invest in anything and the same player using the higher levels of the path end up with nowhere near enough successes to actually reach the higher aspect ceiling.</li> <li>If the Example: I showed was using the normal rules, the sorcerer would be casting at difficulty 9(have 1-2 successes average) while needing to spend 4 successes on top of the initial success to actually cast the spell to do a full 10 dice of damage. That 5 success spell would also be limited to 1 target at touch range and couldn't do anything fancier than lethal damage because the sorcerer would have Nothing to spend on other aspects.</li> </ol></li> </ol></li> <li>Making the dice-pools for casting Ability + Path rating and paths cost current rating x5 to lower XP costs because the above tweaks still leave sorcerer paths generally weaker than the equivalent of a splat's abilities at the same rating. This makes it so sorcerers can be more generalist with a lot of tricks up their sleeves even with generally weaker powers.</li> <li>Use lost tower resonance rules from mage 2nd edition. Resonance raises the dice-pool of path casting by +1 for one type of action and subtracts from the dice-pool by -1 for the opposite type of action for every dot in that resonance. A person with a Fiery resonance would be Really good at spells dealing with fire, renewal, and purification, but would Suck at spells dealing with Ice, water, calm, and temperance.</li> <li>Actually giving Enchanting and Alchemy Rules rather than handing the player a list of example and going &quot;Figure it out&quot;.<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Enchanting allows a player to make an object that either A. Gives [path rating used] dice to a specialist ability roll, B. Gives [1/2 path rating rounded down] successes to a roll, or C. puts a pre-made spell or ritual from another path onto an object for instant access[maximum path rating of the spell or ritual must be less than or equal to the enchanter's path rating]. Aspect are split between how long the enchantment lasts, number of uses, &quot;Price&quot; of use(success added lowers the severity, 1 success may make you kill a person between every use, 5 would be something trivial, 6 would be free), and if enchanting a spell from another path, any aspects used in that spell(enchanting is an extended roll, so a player can still make something stronger than they could normally cast on the fly).</li> <li>Alchemy is allows a player to transmute substances, allowing more complex effects at each level, higher level allowing a player to transmute supernatural substances, which allows a user to copy other splats abilities to a limited extent(or fully become one of them at path level 6). Aspects are the same as enchanting, only instead of copying a &quot;Spell from another path&quot; a sorcerer copies a supernatural ability at a rate of 2 successes per level of ability(maximum half path rating rounded up). As a materials-based path, alchemy can't transmute fully intangible things like like ghosts, spirits, demons, or raw mana, and can't copy the powers of such entities(basically same limitation as Srev).</li> </ol></li> </ol>There are other changes, but this post is long as-is.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That seems very interesting! Could you send me the complete system inbox? I'm thiking of using it for an idea of what might happen in the future (of one of my games), also it seems nice to empower sorcerers. Thanks for taking the time to write it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-08T19:02:54-07:00","id":1483433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483266-thoughts-on-plot-device?p=1483426#post1483426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That seems very interesting! Could you send me the complete system inbox? I'm thiking of using it for an idea of what might happen in the future (of one of my games), also it seems nice to empower sorcerers. Thanks for taking the time to write it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I've got you fam. First I've got to search through the disorganized mess that is my ST notes folder for the lib document I can copy the full list from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-09T01:04:08-07:00","id":1483447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483266-thoughts-on-plot-device#post1483266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, how do you feel about these issues?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the Plot Device in those books is less the issue and more a symptom. It could have been done well.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27252-hades\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27252\" data-vbnamecard=\"27252\">Hades</a> has a point in that the old saying holds true: if you stat it, it can be killed. I know you can create really powerhouse sheets for the NPCs, but there's always the chance that a combination of combo and lucky/unlucky rolls will settle matters in unexpected ways.<br /> <br /> But then you can fudge rolls behind the shield as easily as you can Plot Device shit, so whatever. You can also Plot Device in constructive ways instead of just killing your PCs, so whatever again. As I said, that's not the real problem.<br /> <br /> The real problem is that they didn't gave STs any advice on how to use those characters outside the strict lines of the railroad adventure.<br /> <br /> Lair of the Hidden stays as my favorite adventure for WoD bar none, and virtually every character in it should be capable of disposing of the coterie by themselves individually. But if the adventure simply said that things will go this or that way, and the Methuselah in the castle will just kill the characters if they &quot;mess up&quot;, it would be just as poorly made as Nights of Prophecy, regardless of it having their stats.<br /> <br /> What made LotH better as an adventure isn't the stats themselves, but the fact that the adventure focus much more on presenting the character, goals, passions and frustrations of the casting, and let the PCs deal with them however they want to. It has extremely limited boundaries, yet it lets you explore those boundaries to your heart's content.<br /> <br /> Do the stats help? Yes. Are they necessary? With enough info on the kind of thing you can expect from them, hardly. They're there less because they're integral to its quality and more, again, as a symptom of the mindset behind it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483266-thoughts-on-plot-device?p=1483353#post1483353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The worst thing about Samuel Haight is that he and his skin-dancers could have been a great concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem with Height was less that he had every splat power, and more that this basically surmised him. Even his creation of the Skin Dancers as a whole became a second thought and he went on to just be a bogey-man with all the powers.<br /> <br /> It holds true for the Mage powers, too. The whole process of the Skin Dancer was interesting, becoming a Ghoul is ok on itself. But the story on how he obtained the powers of a Mage isn't bad because he did it, but because it felt cheap. Plot Armor isn't a problem, but it can't <i>feel</i> like it for the reader, and it felt. Likewise, giving a source of power to the character just because you want them to have it isn't at all a problem, but the reader shouldn't <i>feel</i> that the whole thing only exists for this purpose. We don't have this feel with the Rite of Sacred Rebirth and how Height developed it, but we do have with his Mage powers.<br /> <br /> Now, for the current Skin-Dancers... I actually find them ok. I think they actually fit better in the setting now than before.<br /> <br /> Basically, the problem with the original version is that it is too similar in role to the Black Spiral Dancers. Between Fomori, Spirits, other monsters like vampires and the BSD, they would just end up being one more antagonist in a game that has no lack of antagonists. It had no reason for the Garou or the players to ever see the Skin Dancers as anything else than another manifestation of the Wyrm, and Kinfolk that became one of them would necessarily be villains, either by disposition or necessity.<br /> <br /> W20 brought then to a grey area that I feel is a lot more conducive for giving them their own niche, despite being mostly undeveloped. They're a new tribe carving their place in the world and seeking for a purpose, they're a too varied bunch from many distinct tribes and situations trying to build a community and culture without the support of shared traditions, they aren't common rejects lost to the tribes, but outsiders that make themselves Garou by sheer drive and want to be accepted by the others while rejecting the Wyrm. I think this is far more compelling than just making them another antagonist, and at the same time they remain a cautionary tale","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-09T17:49:48-07:00","id":1483530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ut then you can fudge rolls behind the shield as easily as you can Plot Device </div> </div> </div>Certainly, but I find it much easier and more &quot;believable&quot; if I have the said character's sheets to back it up. In any case, I rarely ever fudge rolls, I like the &quot;chaos factor&quot; involved in making the rolls, etc, so that's also another reason I prefer to have the character's sheets. Among other reasons, because I don't like the idea of an &quot;invincible guy&quot;, I prefer the approach of having a fitting character sheet for the character, how hard he is to &quot;kill&quot; is going to be there in the system, so to speak.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> instead of just killing your PCs </div> </div> </div>This is one sensitive topic for sure, but I've always been of the opinion that players must feel that they are in danger of being killed. In general, if you create an environment where the PCs feel they're safe, it not only hurts the immersion among other things, but can also create bad habits in the players. I also hate adventures that say &quot;don't kill PCs&quot;, I guess any ST worth his salt doesn't like the idea of PC's dying (and I'm no exception, I usually hate when it happens), but the possibility of it happening is of uttermost importance for a good story, in my opinion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The real problem is that they didn't gave STs any advice on how to use those characters outside the strict lines of the railroad adventure </div> </div> </div>Exactly! I've always hated extreme railroading, as happen in many WoD stories.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> but because it felt cheap. Plot Armor isn't a problem, but it can't <i>feel</i> like it for the reader, and it felt. Likewise, giving a source of power to the character just because you want them to have it isn't at all a problem, but the reader shouldn't <i>feel</i> that the whole thing only exists for this purpose. We don't have this feel with the Rite of Sacred Rebirth and how Height developed it, but we do have with his Mage powers. </div> </div> </div>You summarized perfectly what I wanted to say (and put it in a much more eloquent way), the problem doesn't lie on the fact that he acquired those powers, but that the way he obtained such powers (Mage Spheres) felt cheap. As I said, we probably wouldn't have the problems we had with Haight if the story of how he obtained such powers wasn't so cheap.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Are they necessary? With enough info on the kind of thing you can expect from them, hardly. </div> </div> </div>In the end, even though I understand your point, I still feel it's better to have the character's traits, as its benefits far outweight the disadvantages, besides, it's fun to create character's sheets lol! I remember when I was a kid, I had a friend that said he considered it the only real pleasure for a ST hahaha...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-09T17:50:29-07:00","id":1483531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483266-thoughts-on-plot-device?p=1483433#post1483433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've got you fam. First I've got to search through the disorganized mess that is my ST notes folder for the lib document I can copy the full list from.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks! I'm anxiously waiting! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-09T19:16:12-07:00","id":1483545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483266-thoughts-on-plot-device?p=1483530#post1483530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Certainly, but I find it much easier and more &quot;believable&quot; if I have the said character's sheets to back it up. In any case, I rarely ever fudge rolls, I like the &quot;chaos factor&quot; involved in making the rolls, etc, so that's also another reason I prefer to have the character's sheets. Among other reasons, because I don't like the idea of an &quot;invincible guy&quot;, I prefer the approach of having a fitting character sheet for the character, how hard he is to &quot;kill&quot; is going to be there in the system, so to speak.</div> </div> </div> </div>Usually I'm the same. My point wasn't so much that this isn't a valid request and I agree that overall it is better to have the character's stats at hand, even if to tweak them. Instead, it was that the lack of sheets wasn't the real cause of the problem, just a symptom of it.<br /> <br /> They didn't let it out because they thought you could figure things out for yourself, they let it out because they didn't want the characters to have a chance, period, and if they had gave a sheet they would still make an adventure that has nothing for you on how to deal with the characters challenging the NPC and winning. They wanted the result of any decision to be to put the party on track as soon as possible or end the adventure entirely.<br /> <br /> Nights of Prophecy is specially guilty of that as in the end it only wants the PCs to be witnesses of the metaplot. It isn't a badly written adventure, it is a badly written tale badly translated into an adventure in the hopes that you'll use your precious game time to tell it to your players, even it having nothing to do with their characters, so they can witness the awesomeness of the author's plot and characters.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483266-thoughts-on-plot-device?p=1483530#post1483530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is one sensitive topic for sure, but I've always been of the opinion that players must feel that they are in danger of being killed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not arguing that, just saying that how this is stated in those adventures is simplistic and doesn't really help.<br /> <br /> What &quot;mess with them&quot; means? A PC can try to confront an NPC in many ways, and even if they come to blows it doesn't has to mean the NPC instantly wants nothing else than kill the PC. They may take any number of other actions depending on circumstances.<br /> <br /> This is specially important for powerful NPCs that don't look so powerful at first glance. As a rule of thumb it is better that those characters take other actions to put the PCs in their place at least at first, but those adventures give none.<br /> <br /> Now, if the PCs do something really risky or really stupid, or just take their chances knowing the stakes and lose, sure, by all means kill them. But compare that with NoP &quot;if there's a Nosferatu PC, Vasilisa kills them, just 'cause&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483266-thoughts-on-plot-device?p=1483530#post1483530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the end, even though I understand your point, I still feel it's better to have the character's traits, as its benefits far outweight the disadvantages, besides, it's fun to create character's sheets lol! I remember when I was a kid, I had a friend that said he considered it the only real pleasure for a ST hahaha...</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. As I said, it was just about the problem presented. But that aside, I also prefer to have a sheet.<br /> <br /> Which is one of the many things I don't like in Ur-Shulgi...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-09T19:37:20-07:00","id":1483547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Usually I'm the same. My point wasn't so much that this isn't a valid request and I agree that overall it is better to have the character's stats at hand, even if to tweak them. Instead, it was that the lack of sheets wasn't the real cause of the problem, just a symptom of it. </div> </div> </div>I see your point, I guess we're on the same page then.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Nights of Prophecy is specially guilty of that as in the end it only wants the PCs to be witnesses of the metaplot </div> </div> </div>I completely agree. I think the story of Baba Yaga's demise (I forgot the name) is one of the worst I've seen in the WoD. It refers to what we were talking about on the subject of Samuel Haight, it feels &quot;forced&quot;, not interesting in the least and extremely railroaded. I mean everything suddenly goes wrong for Baba Yaga, she loses her entire army, and it feels it's all for the purpose of the setting getting rid of Baba Yaga, it doesn't flow naturally. This, besides the even more appalling fact that the PCs can't do a thing about it, their actions are COMPLETELY irrelevant, what's the point of an adventure like that?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Which is one of the many things I don't like in Ur-Shulgi... </div> </div> </div>I also never understood his character sheet, I mean what's the point of making such character sheet if it mostly made with vague statements that are sometimes even hard to interpret, like:<br /> <i>Thaumaturgical Paths: Unknown; presumably godlike proficiency in the ancient practices...</i><br /> <br /> I mean, what is that supposed to mean?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12348,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","user":"Herr Meister","date":". 06-10-2022, 10:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-09T21:07:42-07:00","id":1483551,"title":"","content":"The true reason for them to get rid of Baba Yaga? They finally noticed that there are players in Russia and that the &quot;Mystical Iron Curtain&quot; was a crappy idea all along.<br /> <br /> But instead of retconing it or making a piece of fiction like the one in Time of Thin Blood, they made that shitty &quot;adventure&quot; where your players are so powerless that their actions hardly change even their own fates in it. I mean, making it a survival story was an option that could have resulted in a better adventure. Instead it is just &quot;Russia: the Exposition&quot;.<br /> <br /> Heck, ToTB's fiction on the demise of Ravnos is actually a fun reading, as gonzo as it is, and I would actively seek to buy an adventure set in the events of the Week of Nightmares just to survive it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}